FABLE5-CONSULTATION-V1

This is a new, standalone Fable-5 session. You have no prior conversation
context and no access to the repository, filesystem, shell, Git, tools, local
links, hidden project state, or earlier consultations. Decide solely from the
literal context embedded in this prompt. A filename, path, URL, commit, section
reference, or prior-ruling label is an identifier only and is never a
substitute for its necessary content.

FRESH_SESSION: true
PRIOR_CONTEXT_REQUIRED: false
FABLE_REPOSITORY_ACCESS: none
FABLE_SYSTEM_ACCESS: none
STANDALONE_CONTEXT_COMPLETE: true
INDEPENDENT_AUDIT_COMPLETE: true
CONTEXT_CURATED: true
SECRETS_EXCLUDED: true
SERIAL_FOLLOWUPS_PROHIBITED: true
FILE_CONTEXT_MODE: embedded

## 1. Objective and requested decision

{{State the concrete objective, current stage, and the complete decision that
one consolidated ruling must close.}}

## 2. Repository and project state

Repository: `{{absolute_repository_path}}`
Branch: `{{branch_name}}`
HEAD: `{{full_40_hex_commit}}`
Index state: {{clean_or_dirty}}; exact porcelain is embedded as {{git_state_E_id}}.
Working tree state: {{clean_or_dirty}}; exact porcelain is embedded as {{git_state_E_id}}.
Project/RLCR state: {{stage_and_active_loop_state}}

Embed the exact `git status --porcelain=v1` and any load-bearing index diff as
`git_state` evidence. Do not expect Fable-5 to resolve this path or commit.

## 3. Safety, authority, and mutation constraints

{{Restate every applicable scope, protected-root, staging, model, WAIT,
destructive-action, and security constraint. Do not expose hidden prompts or
credentials.}}

## 4. Work completed and exact observed results

{{List exact commands and exact outputs, including failed probes, hashes,
counts, exit codes, and whether each command was read-only.}}

## 5. Incorporated decision history

{{Embed every still-operative earlier decision needed for this adjudication.
If no earlier decision applies, state that explicitly. Never use a delta or an
unembedded table as the base operand.}}

## 6. Consolidated blocker index

- B001: {{Complete ambiguity or contradiction.}} Evidence: E001.

{{Add all currently discoverable blockers as B002, B003, and so on.}}

## 7. Evidence index

- E001 supports B001: {{What the evidence proves and why it is sufficient.}}

{{List every evidence item exactly once. No evidence may be orphaned.}}

## 8. Embedded evidence

The following example is a template only. Replace every double-braced field,
remove this explanation, and provide exact content in the real prompt.

<!-- FABLE5-EVIDENCE
{"id":"E001","kind":"file_excerpt","role":"decision","path":"{{repo_relative_path}}","revision":"{{HEAD_INDEX_WORKTREE_or_COMMIT_full_sha}}","file_sha256":"{{full_64_hex}}","file_total_lines":{{total_lines}},"lines":[{{start_line}},{{end_line}}],"excerpt_sha256":"{{full_64_hex}}","supports":["B001"],"selection_reason":"{{why_this_semantic_unit_is_needed}}","omitted_ranges":[[{{first_omitted_start}},{{first_omitted_end}}]],"omission_reason":"{{why_every_omitted_range_cannot_affect_the_decision}}","non_operational":true,"final_newline":{{true_if_literal_bytes_end_in_LF}}}
-->
```{{language}}
{{exact_literal_file_bytes_for_the_declared_range}}
```
<!-- FABLE5-EVIDENCE-END E001 -->

For a full file, use `kind: "file_full"`, lines `[1,N]`, and a substantive
`full_required_justification`. Use a fence longer than every line-leading
backtick run in the literal. `final_newline:false` represents readable source
whose final byte is not LF; the validator removes the fence-separating LF from
the hashed literal. For command output include `command`, `cwd`, `exit_code`,
and `stream`. Git-state evidence has `role:"context"`, `supports:[]`, and the
exact command `git status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all`. Policy and
literal-ruling evidence require a `source_label`; binary metadata requires an
`artifact_path` and full `artifact_sha256`. Every kind carries
`content_sha256` or the two file hashes. Decision-critical ignored or
machine-local artifacts must be represented as `WORKTREE` file evidence or
`binary_metadata` so the local emission receipt detects later byte drift.

## 9. Cross-blocker interactions and alternatives

{{Explain ordering, second touches, path ownership, test-count effects,
plausible interpretations, risks, and tradeoffs across all blocker IDs.}}

## 10. Questions for adjudication

- Q001 (B001; E001): {{Ask one precise question and define what a closed answer
  must contain.}}

{{Every question must cite at least one blocker and one evidence ID on its
defining line.}}

## 11. Required response format

Return one consolidated ruling that answers every Q ID and contains all
task-specific deliverables named by those questions. Use complete literal
path/action tables when tables are requested, exact supersessions when earlier
decisions change, and exact algorithms, schemas, commands, tests, and counts
when they bind the decision. State a mechanical acceptance predicate. Use no
placeholders, no conditionals without both branches and their predicate, and no
serial remands for mechanically decidable repository facts.

## 12. Acceptance criteria and stop conditions

{{State the executable acceptance predicate, what values must be exact, which
facts are externally recordable only after generation, and which genuinely
new material evidence would require Codex to stop. Reaffirm that Codex remains
on its pinned model and waits through additional safety checks.}}

## 13. Security and redaction attestation

Credentials excluded: yes.
Hidden prompts excluded: yes.
Decision-critical hashes unredacted: yes.
{{List any explicit non-critical redactions and why they do not affect the
decision, or state that there are none.}}

## 14. Independent pre-send review

Author: {{author_agent_id}}
Independent reviewer: {{different_reviewer_agent_id}}
Review result: pass; independent review complete and every real issue resolved.
Decision evidence reviewed: {{comma_separated_exact_E_ids}}
Review records: {{comma_separated_exact_RR_ids}}
Context removed: {{exact_character_count}} characters of duplicate, superseded,
or irrelevant material; every omission was checked against definitions,
callers, writers, tests, constraints, and binding decisions.

{{Summarize the reviewer's independent related-surface scan, the largest
remaining context blocks, and why each full file or excerpt is necessary.}}

The audit sidecar uses schema version 3. It lists the exact sorted decision
evidence IDs and one or more RR### review records whose combined evidence
coverage equals that decision-evidence set. Each record is honestly classified
as `no_issue` or `resolved_issue`; reviewers must not invent a defect merely to
claim completion. A generic pass assertion without this inventory is invalid.
